    "title": "pandas.Index.inferred_type — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.inferred_type#\n\n- Index.inferred_type[source]#\n- Return a string of the type inferred from the values. This inspects the actual values in the Index to determine their type, which may differ from the stored `dtype` . For example,\nan object-dtype Index containing only integers returns`'integer'` .See also \n  - `Index.dtype`\n  - Return the dtype object of the underlying data.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.Index([1, 2, 3]) >>> idx Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int64') >>> idx.inferred_type 'integer'",
